      "claim": "Compound Z18483535 has human oral bioavailability of 55.7%, above the 20% threshold, supporting high F.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "The query is warfarin, a lipophilic 4-hydroxycoumarin with a phenyl-butanone side chain. Multiple structurally related or similarly lipophilic acidic oral drugs (ketoprofen, diflunisal, baclofen, felbamate) show high oral bioavailability (74-92%), while the low-bioavailability comparators are highly polar or polyphenolic and not representative. Therefore F >= 20% is strongly supported.",
